          "path": "_m/f/0/5/k/waugoshance-light-wp/waugoshance-lighthouse-an-aban.jpg",
          "filename": "Waugoshance Lighthouse, an abandoned lighthouse in northern Lake Michigan.jpg",
          "caption": "The oldest lighthouse on the Great Lakes completely surrounded by water, Waugoshance Lighthouse is slowly losing the battle of the elements to Lake Huron. Built in 1851, it has withstood the ravages of time, wind, waves and even withstood bombing practice during World War II. This image shows the lighthouses' west flank with a tower of the Mighty Mackinaw Bridge peering out of the horizon 18 miles to the east in the Mackinaw Straits.",
          "alt": "The oldest lighthouse on the Great Lakes completely surrounded by water, Waugoshance Lighthouse is slowly losing the battle of the elements to Lake Huron. Built in 1851, it has withstood the ravages of time, wind, waves and even withstood bombing practice during World War II. This image shows the lighthouses' west flank with a tower of the Mighty Mackinaw Bridge peering out of the horizon 18 miles to the east in the Mackinaw Straits.",
          "width": 4122,
          "height": 3092,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
          "artist": "William ORourke",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Waugoshance_Lighthouse,_an_abandoned_lighthouse_in_northern_Lake_Michigan.jpg",
